# systemd-tmpfiles snapshot

These files were extracted from the uploaded `tmpfiles.d.zip` archive and kept here as reference material for the Fire4Nix / ROCKNIX beta pass.

They are reference-only. The useful part of this snapshot is the expanded set of tmpfiles rules, which helps cross-check:
- cleanup and cache directories;
- network and accessibility defaults;
- X11 / Xorg helper cleanup;
- BlueZ / systemd / provision rules.

## Captured files

- `README`
- `connectivity.conf`
- `credstore.conf`
- `dbus.conf`
- `journal-nocow.conf`
- `legacy.conf`
- `provision.conf`
- `retroarch-userdirs.conf`
- `static-nodes-permissions.conf`
- `systemd-pstore.conf`
- `systemd-resolve.conf`
- `systemd-tmp.conf`
- `systemd.conf`
- `tmp.conf`
- `var.conf`
- `x11.conf`
- `z_01_rocknix.conf`
- `z_05_bluez.conf`
- `z_90_xorg-server.conf`

The files live under `rocknix_reference/etc/tmpfiles.d/` so the project stays self-contained.
